.{
    .name = .phux_cockpit,
    .fingerprint = 0xa47a656ea288c810,
    .version = "0.16.1", // x-release-please-version
    .minimum_zig_version = "0.16.0",
    .dependencies = .{
        // Native v0.8.1 plus Cockpit's terminal fixes, plus the render work
        // on `fix/terminal-render-cliff`.
        //
        // The headline is `CanvasCommand.cell_grid`: a terminal is now ONE
        // packed lattice of 20-byte cells that each renderer expands, instead
        // of per-run rects and text. A display list cannot hold a dense
        // terminal — a distinct fg+bg per cell merges nothing, so a 200x60
        // screen wanted ~24,000 commands at ~696 B of retained mirror each,
        // and the painter silently truncated from the bottom: 9 of 60 rows.
        // It is now 60 of 60 in 4 commands, and 300x100 fits in 585 KB.
        // Cluster bytes are interned, so text cost tracks the alphabet rather
        // than the cell count.
        //
        // Two bug classes close by construction: one retained key replaced
        // wholesale means no per-run command can be orphaned when a row loses
        // a run (the stale glyphs a widening pane left behind), and position
        // IS the index, so a fallback glyph cannot shift its row off the grid.
        // Every SGR attribute finally has somewhere to live.
        //
        // The grid is emitted one command PER ROW, not one per screen. A
        // retained command is the unit of change, so a screen-wide grid would
        // have made every keystroke re-encode every cell — moving the
        // full-surface cost from the rasterizer to the wire rather than
        // removing it. Cluster interning is per-row for the same reason:
        // per-screen interning put every row's fingerprint on every other
        // row's characters, and one new letter re-encoded the screen (measured
        // at 31 upserts / 8449 bytes a frame before the fix, 1 upsert and
        // ~400-800 bytes after).
        //
        // With the AppKit decoder and wire v6, terminal frames are back on the
        // GPU packet path with incremental patching, which the CPU fallback
        // had disabled entirely:
        //   gpu_present_path    pixels -> packet
        //   present_mode        none   -> patch
        //   present_patch_bytes 0      -> 789 (one upsert on a prompt)
        //   input latency       19.4ms -> 5.36ms, against a 16.67ms budget
        //
        // The per-view command ceiling also went back 4096 -> 2048: terminals
        // were the only reason it was raised, and one now costs ~100 commands.
        // A cell grid also carries a font FAMILY — regular plus bold, italic,
        // and bold-italic ids — and both renderers select per cell off the
        // style flags, so one row mixes weights. Where a companion face is not
        // registered the renderers synthesize identically from one shared rule
        // (faux bold double-strikes, faux italic shears about the baseline),
        // because a bold run that renders bold on the reference path and plain
        // on the host is worse than no bold at all.
        // Secondary windows can finally paint. Every terminal cell comes from
        // `chrome.build`, and the toolkit installed an app-owned chrome
        // display list for the MAIN canvas only — a second window rendered its
        // tab strip and divider with zero terminal cells. `build_window` takes
        // a `ChromeContext` naming the window, `rebuildWindowSlot` installs
        // through it, and `on_frame` now runs per slot so a secondary
        // window's terminals are actually resized. Additive: an app that has
        // not migrated is unchanged, because the branch is gated on
        // `build_window` rather than on `chrome`.
        //
        // Also adds the fullscreen verb the platform layer never had. It
        // REPORTED `WindowInfo.fullscreen` and had no way to enter or leave —
        // and the field it reported was never filled by anything, so it was a
        // constant false.
        //
        // REBASED onto upstream v0.9.0, and carries four more Cockpit fixes:
        //
        // - macOS font smoothing is set explicitly for every glyph raster
        //   context. THIS MOVES ZERO PIXELS, and the claim that used to stand
        //   here — "off by default on a transparent backing ... +35% solid
        //   stem pixels" — was measured wrong and is false. The two states
        //   that actually shipped are identical to four decimal places:
        //
        //     e8bd84886 (calls ABSENT)  cell_grid mean_luma=45.7978 solid=4179
        //     f3678832f (calls `true`)  cell_grid mean_luma=45.7978 solid=4179
        //
        //   The +35% came from comparing the pin against a LOCAL EDIT that set
        //   the calls to `false` — a state no build was ever in. Absent
        //   defaults to smoothing ENABLED on these contexts, so there was
        //   nothing to turn on. Keep the calls: they pin the behaviour against
        //   a future default change. Do not credit them with a fix.
        //   Re-measure two REAL commits with `scripts/host-raster-compare.sh`,
        //   never a hand-edited counterfactual. See phux-cockpit-aht.
        // - `web_panes` takes a `ChromeContext`, like `build_window`. Panes
        //   are reconciled PER WINDOW, so a signature that could not say which
        //   window it was being asked about made every OTHER window's rebuild
        //   resolve the webview anchor against a tree without it and log a
        //   warning. BREAKING: implementors take the context (see
        //   `view.webPanes`, which now answers only for the main window).
        // - Automation snapshots drop CLOSED windows. A closed window keeps
        //   its runtime slot, so the snapshot published ghost `window @wN`
        //   lines with no views under them, which would quietly pass any smoke
        //   test asserting a window count.
        // - `widget-key` emits a paired key_up. The harness sent only
        //   key_down, so the shortcut latch swallowed every repeated chord —
        //   driving cmd+G twice did nothing the second time.
        // - `semantics.decorative` splits announcement from visibility.
        //   `hidden` suppresses RENDERING (and still reserves layout), which
        //   is why the search field's magnifier and caret painted nothing
        //   until it was removed from both; `decorative` paints and hides from
        //   accessibility instead.
        // - `fx.openUrl(url)` opens a URL in the user's default handler from
        //   `update`. The platform seam already reached NSWorkspace; nothing
        //   app-facing was wired to it, so the only callers were the webview
        //   bridge and a runtime path gated on webview link policy. Validated
        //   against a scheme ALLOWLIST (http, https, mailto) with control
        //   bytes and whitespace refused whole rather than trimmed — this is
        //   the second of two gates in front of terminal output, the first
        //   being Cockpit's own URL detection.
        //
        // What the v0.9.0 base adds that this app actually calls. The pin
        // moved for these, not for the version number:
        //
        // - `fx.showNotification(.{ .title, .subtitle, .body })`, so a bell
        //   that rings while the app is in the background reaches the person
        //   who is not looking at it. Fire-and-forget by construction: the OS
        //   owns whether the banner is shown, so no success Msg would be true.
        // - `Options.status_item_fn`, the `web_panes` shape for a menu-bar
        //   extra: consulted after every rebuild, re-applied only when its
        //   output changed, with the title and the menu patched independently.
        //   Items dispatch `command` strings through the same `on_command`
        //   table the menu bar and the shortcut registrations already use.
        // - `fx.minimizeWindow` / `fx.hideWindow`, the two verbs the platform
        //   layer had no app-facing seam for. Supplying custom menus replaces
        //   the stock bar, so an app that declares menus and cannot perform
        //   these is an app whose cmd+M does nothing.
        // - `Options.on_pinch` (`platform.PinchEvent`, multiplicative
        //   per-event deltas) and `Options.on_drop` (`platform.FileDropEvent`,
        //   paths plus the view-local point), the trackpad and Finder seams a
        //   terminal is expected to answer.
        // - `Options.on_appearance` (`platform.Appearance`), which is how
        //   `theme = auto` can follow the system without polling anything.
        // - A 32-slot PTY effect table, matching Cockpit's bounded terminal
        //   registry instead of silently binding the whole app at four shells.
        //
        // cockpit/v0.9.5 (2026-09-02): the same Cockpit commits rebased onto
        // upstream v0.9.5, plus the seam the TypeScript migration needs:
        //
        // - `AppOptions.native_extension`, an app-owned Zig module the
        //   generated core.ts runner calls to compose `host_calls`, the
        //   view/markup options and the final `native_sdk.App`. Cockpit's
        //   `typescript-spike/src/native_extension.zig` reserves the
        //   `cockpit.` command namespace through the generalized
        //   `HostCallMux` and keeps a real engine behind it.
        // - `AppArtifacts.extension`, `.test_extension` and
        //   `.extension_tests`: Zig collects tests from the root module only,
        //   so an extension's guards need their own test artifact, and a Zig
        //   module can only import below its own root, so the app's build
        //   hands the engine to each instance as a module.
        // - Comptime markup diagnostics name the markup again instead of
        //   failing on Zig 0.16's refusal to discard an error value.
        // - Split widgets carry an axis through layout, pointer drag, keyboard
        //   steps, resize cursor, paint, and accessibility while preserving
        //   horizontal as the source-compatible default.
        // - The runtime's existing scoped display-list refresh batch is public.
        //   Cockpit uses `beginCanvasWidgetDisplayListRefreshBatch`/`end...`
        //   only around the installing main-canvas event: display-list work and
        //   presentation stay synchronous, while AppKit accessibility
        //   publication moves to the responding frame's post-present flush.
        // - Whole-file writes open or create the requested parent before
        //   touching the destination, preserve final symlink entries, retain
        //   confinement through verified parent handles, and stream special
        //   files through the exact no-follow-opened handle.
        .native_sdk = .{
            .url = "https://github.com/phall1/native/archive/71bbce511187b9e071d3ca8cbf3b1b19138577da.tar.gz",
            .hash = "native_sdk-0.1.0-hzDzQuqdsgJPbC6HFzLKzGhOB2EWgKfiNTcSOjK9WCMO",
        },
        // libghostty-vt: Ghostty's extracted terminal-state core, consumed
        // as the `ghostty-vt` Zig module. Pinned to the first upstream
        // commit that builds under Zig 0.16.0 (the "Update to Zig 0.16.0"
        // merge); simd is disabled at import so the module stays pure Zig.
        .ghostty = .{
            .url = "https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty/archive/7aa9591746ffa4d2eee458960c76554352832595.tar.gz",
            .hash = "ghostty-1.3.2-dev-5UdBC-edJAVXTdYsgHOzIqgAI7hE8VqpmriEi8zgufw2",
        },
    },
    .paths = .{ "build.zig", "build.zig.zon", "src", "app.zon", "version.txt", "assets", "scripts", "README.md", "CHANGELOG.md", "LICENSE", "THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md" },
}
